[[:db/retract 17592186314744 :question/answer-fields 17592186314169] [:db/retract 17592186314744 :question/answer-fields 17592186314418] {:db/id 17592186365858 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10\\lambda {y}^{′}+25{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,y(2)+2{y}^{′}(2)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\lambda \\in R.\n$$\n\nFind the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of this problem. Assume that $B$ and $C$ are constants." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314744 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-12\\lambda {y}^{′}+36{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,y(1)+2{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\lambda \\in R.\n$$\n\nFind the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of this problem. Assume that $B$ and $C$ are constants." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8dd2d3fa-c650-5e37-9b97-e79bceb3c6ba" "answer-field-9b93007b-725a-5c21-aef1-4108c8c123fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8dd2d3fa-c650-5e37-9b97-e79bceb3c6ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd2d3fa-c650-5e37-9b97-e79bceb3c6ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-900413a5-3275-52e8-aad8-708d3d20a529" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b6a8205-b73b-5687-a756-4e7c12880207" "answer-28512bc4-3366-5851-ab15-e9ddf7bdc6ed" "answer-9df526c7-25b8-5eaf-9168-18db96d42a4e" "answer-900413a5-3275-52e8-aad8-708d3d20a529"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b6a8205-b73b-5687-a756-4e7c12880207" :answer/id #uuid "3b6a8205-b73b-5687-a756-4e7c12880207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28512bc4-3366-5851-ab15-e9ddf7bdc6ed" :answer/id #uuid "28512bc4-3366-5851-ab15-e9ddf7bdc6ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9df526c7-25b8-5eaf-9168-18db96d42a4e" :answer/id #uuid "9df526c7-25b8-5eaf-9168-18db96d42a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{12}$ and $\\frac{1}{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-900413a5-3275-52e8-aad8-708d3d20a529" :answer/id #uuid "900413a5-3275-52e8-aad8-708d3d20a529" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac{1}{12}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b93007b-725a-5c21-aef1-4108c8c123fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b93007b-725a-5c21-aef1-4108c8c123fb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f6353e39-4783-54e8-b20e-f618126b98a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33bd6051-1ce7-59a0-a89b-5f289fa49519" "answer-2ed3b012-ea23-5630-95d6-c16372fcd823" "answer-f6353e39-4783-54e8-b20e-f618126b98a2" "answer-408a492f-a860-5962-a306-84c6d1f01f6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33bd6051-1ce7-59a0-a89b-5f289fa49519" :answer/id #uuid "33bd6051-1ce7-59a0-a89b-5f289fa49519" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{-2x}$ and $C{e}^{x}(x-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ed3b012-ea23-5630-95d6-c16372fcd823" :answer/id #uuid "2ed3b012-ea23-5630-95d6-c16372fcd823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{-x}$ and $C{e}^{x}(x-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6353e39-4783-54e8-b20e-f618126b98a2" :answer/id #uuid "f6353e39-4783-54e8-b20e-f618126b98a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B{e}^{-x}(x+1)$ and $C{e}^{x/2}(x-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-408a492f-a860-5962-a306-84c6d1f01f6b" :answer/id #uuid "408a492f-a860-5962-a306-84c6d1f01f6b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B{e}^{-x}(x-1)$ and $C{e}^{x/2}(x-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166940 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-827b7203-4bc8-5ef4-ada5-12343dfe7439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186391695 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-827b7203-4bc8-5ef4-ada5-12343dfe7439" :question/id #uuid "827b7203-4bc8-5ef4-ada5-12343dfe7439" :question/math-academy-id "q-338917" :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9\\lambda y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda >0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions ${y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields $A=0.$ Thus, we have a nontrivial solution, so $\\lambda =0$ is a parameter corresponding to eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+9\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 3\\text{i}\\sqrt{\\lambda }.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3B\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $B=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(3)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-3A\\sqrt{\\lambda }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n9\\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{81}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-314046e0-b3cb-5409-b06d-bb0e8f9f90c3" "answer-field-6c50717b-94b2-5e1c-9cdd-e60b58c14e94"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-314046e0-b3cb-5409-b06d-bb0e8f9f90c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "314046e0-b3cb-5409-b06d-bb0e8f9f90c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3a127422-744b-580f-8766-eedd4918927a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9863903c-b7b0-5c31-8d4c-bcb8da7c8123" "answer-333487d5-2b4f-53f7-a1f4-c935ce9920e2" "answer-3a127422-744b-580f-8766-eedd4918927a" "answer-3d8a953c-29a1-5c31-b0ad-482482bf1033"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9863903c-b7b0-5c31-8d4c-bcb8da7c8123" :answer/id #uuid "9863903c-b7b0-5c31-8d4c-bcb8da7c8123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-333487d5-2b4f-53f7-a1f4-c935ce9920e2" :answer/id #uuid "333487d5-2b4f-53f7-a1f4-c935ce9920e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a127422-744b-580f-8766-eedd4918927a" :answer/id #uuid "3a127422-744b-580f-8766-eedd4918927a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{81}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d8a953c-29a1-5c31-b0ad-482482bf1033" :answer/id #uuid "3d8a953c-29a1-5c31-b0ad-482482bf1033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c50717b-94b2-5e1c-9cdd-e60b58c14e94" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c50717b-94b2-5e1c-9cdd-e60b58c14e94" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-74d7d903-23a2-5c49-b052-79f08cba23e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74d7d903-23a2-5c49-b052-79f08cba23e5" "answer-a7739e90-7698-5078-912c-cda3c5ade6a3" "answer-0e54c974-6252-5708-b98d-d9bcad440480" "answer-f8cb5d6d-8680-580b-b06c-9309df73f9bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74d7d903-23a2-5c49-b052-79f08cba23e5" :answer/id #uuid "74d7d903-23a2-5c49-b052-79f08cba23e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7739e90-7698-5078-912c-cda3c5ade6a3" :answer/id #uuid "a7739e90-7698-5078-912c-cda3c5ade6a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e54c974-6252-5708-b98d-d9bcad440480" :answer/id #uuid "0e54c974-6252-5708-b98d-d9bcad440480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8cb5d6d-8680-580b-b06c-9309df73f9bc" :answer/id #uuid "f8cb5d6d-8680-580b-b06c-9309df73f9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186391720 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16\\lambda y=0,\\,y(0)=y(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
